    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Exelon Business Services Company (BSC) invests in corporate-owned life insurance for the purpose of funding future payments related to an executive compensation program. As of December 31, 2024, the cash surrender value of the insurance purchased was $1,658,208 which was invested with Pacific Life.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">BSC holds investments in Rabbi Trusts for the purpose of funding future payments related to employee and director deferred compensation. As of December 31, 2024, $56,784,186 was held in a Rabbi Trust administered by Northern Trust.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Exelon Business Services Company (BSC) invests in corporate-owned life insurance for the purpose of funding future payments related to an executive compensation program. As of December 31, 2025, the cash surrender value of the insurance purchased was $1,726,831 which was invested with Pacific Life.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">BSC holds investments in Rabbi Trusts for the purpose of funding future payments related to employee and director deferred compensation. As of December 31, 2025, $63,875,916 was held in a Rabbi Trust administered by Northern Trust.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In 2015, BSC entered into a 10-year perpetual user software licensing agreement (&#8220;PULA&#8221;) with Oracle Corporation, ending in 2025. Which provided BSC and Exelon&#8217;s operating companies with the right to use any Oracle software license and required Oracle to provide license maintenance services. The right to use Oracle's licenses over the life of the agreement was determined to be a limited-term intangible asset and thus has been presented in FERC Account 186. Amortization of the asset has been recorded to FERC Account 404.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Net income/loss primarily relates to unrealized losses/gains on the assets in the Rabbi Trust.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
